1374:
The City of Valdosta has a business need to augment traditional communication methods with the use of social media platforms. The use of social media can be beneficial when it facilitates further discussion of city issues, operations and services by providing members of the public the opportunity to participate in local government via the internet. Authorized city employees have the ability to publish articles, facilitate discussions and communicate information through various social media platforms conducive to city business. When used in accordance with applicable laws, regulations and policies as well as prudent operational, security, and privacy considerations, social media platforms can:
(1) Enhance the speed, reach, and target of communications (particularly during disaster/emergency incidents);
(2) Facilitate collaboration;
(3) Improve information exchange between residents and employees;
(4) Increase citizens' engagement and dialogue;
(5) Streamline processes;
(6) Foster productivity improvements; and
(7) Increase the city's ability to broadcast messages to the widest possible audience.
(Ord. No. 2018-26, 10-25-2018)
